REMARK Chain B has multiple CYS disulfides, with B5-B6 adjacent residue         
REMARK disulfide. (should test adjacent disulfide link with TAIL-HEAD unlinked) 
REMARK Cains A and C are Zwitterion form CYS and linked across chain B          
REMARK   (discontiguous molecules test)                                         
REMARK Chain B N-term is HYP (there is no N-term HYP in main libs,              
REMARK                         but I found that GLYCAM has one)                 
REMARK ASP B12 and B14 are ASH                                                  
REMARK TER insterted between B17, B18 to force a break where there realy is none
REMARK LYS B10 NZ is linked to DG D1 P                                          
REMARK ASN B20 ND2 is linked to NAG F1 C1                                       
REMARK CYS B24 is CYM                                                           
REMARK GLY B28 is terminal carboxyl with HXT                                    
REMARK HYP B1 OD1 islinked to MAN C1 C1                                         
REMARK NAG F1 links at O4, branches at O6                                       
REMARK BMA F3 links at O3, branches at O6                                       
REMARK Chain G is a circular peptide, missing hydrogens                         
REMARK G47 has altLoc                                                           
REMARK LYS G52 side chain is truncated at CG                                    
REMARK ARG G53 side chain collides with TRP G57                                 
REMARK G45=LYN, G48=CYM, G49=ASH, G50=GLH                                       
REMARK Chain I is a heparin type sulfated sugar (SGN,IDS), initiated with NPO   
REMARK Phosphotyrosine PTR G39 P links to DNA H1-H2                             
REMARK -- which would be simpler modelled as standard Tyrosine linked to 5'P DNA
REMARK GFP chromophore: G66 CR2; AMBER lib leaprc.xFPchromophores has CR2, but  
REMARK hydrogens need rename: H1-H10->HA31,HA32,HD2,HE2,HE1,HD1,HB2,HA11,HA12,H)
REMARK chain J is circular RNA                                                  
REMARK Residue K1 is an enormous 439 atom single residue ligand                 
REMARK Residue K2 has a numeric name 017                                        
REMARK Residue K3 HETID = PTL, COMP_ID = A1PTL tagged as HETNAM overflow field  
REMARK and as hetsyn COMP_ID:<name> (test long name handling and HETNAM,HETSYN) 
REMARK Residue K4 is a weird sugar that really needs hybrid GLYCAM+GAFF         
REMARK                                                                          
REMARK Missing:                                                                 
REMARK    * Weird sequential non N-C amino acid linkages e.g. IAS               
REMARK    * insertion codes                                                     
REMARK                                                                          
REMARK Note on handling long standard resNames. There are two residue forms:    
REMARK ATOM and HETATM. ATOM records ar globally defined types (well known,     
REMARK no dictinary needed) with 3-letter code = resName. HETATM types are      
REMARK everything else, with 3-letter code = HetID, which in theory is unique   
REMARK only at the *file* level, with unique identification in HETNAM, HETSYN.  
REMARK this allows for a human-meanigful residue code indeatd of a random       
REMARK dtabase key. But given lazy programming HetID is now  arandom database   
REMARK key COMP_ID, which now reauires more thsan 3 characters for uniqueness.  
REMARK                                                                          
REMARK Given that new 5-letter codes start with A1, and will be sequential      
REMARK beause it is random garbage, COMP_ID should be left-                     
REMARK truncated for better chance of unique 3-letter code. Otherwise user      
REMARK defined, or possibly randomized by incrment to avoid conflicts.          
REMARK                                                                          
REMARK There is no standard COMP_ID designation. As an ugly hack extension,     
REMARK some softares place the long name past the text field in HETNAM (70-80). 
REMARK Far more sensible is to use the standards-defined HETSYN.                
REMARK HETSYN is a list of semicolon delimited names. <label>:<value>;          
REMARK is typical for PDB lists, so this form is optimal standards conforming.  
HETNAM     PTL Pritelivir                                            A1BXB      
HETSYN     PTL COMP_ID:A1BXB; N-methyl-N-(4-methyl-5-sulfamoyl-1,3-             
HETSYN   2 PTL thiazol-2-yl)-2-[4-(pyridin-2-yl)phenyl]acetamide                
